WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:03.330
- So Sophia and Sofia's
characters are friends who are set

00:00:03.330 --> 00:00:04.860
up to be enemies.

00:00:04.860 --> 00:00:06.360
How do you think the dynamic

00:00:06.360 --> 00:00:09.120
of that kind of plays out
in real world as well?

00:00:09.120 --> 00:00:12.246
'Cause I felt like,

00:00:12.246 --> 00:00:14.310
and maybe it's just in the musician world

00:00:14.310 --> 00:00:16.230
I don't know if it's the
same in the acting world

00:00:16.230 --> 00:00:19.320
but they always try and pit
females against each other.

00:00:19.320 --> 00:00:20.285
They do in the music world at least.

00:00:20.285 --> 00:00:21.237
- I think in the world at large.

00:00:21.237 --> 00:00:23.130
And I thought that was
kind of interesting.

00:00:23.130 --> 00:00:24.870
- It's funny, yesterday
we were doing an interview

00:00:24.870 --> 00:00:25.837
and somebody said,

00:00:25.837 --> 00:00:27.540
"You guys have such
great chemistry up there,

00:00:27.540 --> 00:00:28.980
did it feel competitive?"

00:00:28.980 --> 00:00:30.240
And we were like, What?

00:00:30.240 --> 00:00:33.050
Like no, It felt so inspiring,

00:00:33.050 --> 00:00:34.500
I think was the word you used.

00:00:34.500 --> 00:00:35.527
Like, which was so great.

00:00:35.527 --> 00:00:39.120
It was, we kept upping
the ante for each other

00:00:39.120 --> 00:00:41.220
and encouraging each other to play

00:00:41.220 --> 00:00:43.266
and find new ways to do the scene.

00:00:43.266 --> 00:00:45.990
It didn't feel competitive at all.

00:00:45.990 --> 00:00:49.740
- There's just been so little
opportunity for us, right?

00:00:49.740 --> 00:00:52.170
And so the little that did come around,

00:00:52.170 --> 00:00:53.310
instead of acknowledging that,

00:00:53.310 --> 00:00:56.130
there was a need for more opportunity,

00:00:56.130 --> 00:00:58.612
they made it about women
not supporting each other.

00:00:58.612 --> 00:00:59.445
- [Kerry] Right.

00:00:59.445 --> 00:01:01.560
- And I think it was the easy way out

00:01:01.560 --> 00:01:05.020
because I have never been more supported

00:01:05.940 --> 00:01:07.710
than by the women in my life,

00:01:07.710 --> 00:01:08.555
- Mm.

00:01:08.555 --> 00:01:10.590
- inspired by the women of my life,

00:01:10.590 --> 00:01:12.900
been brave because of
the women in my life.

00:01:12.900 --> 00:01:14.730
So we just need more opportunity.

00:01:14.730 --> 00:01:15.900
We need-

00:01:15.900 --> 00:01:16.733
- [Kelly] That's what I-

00:01:16.733 --> 00:01:17.861
- I love being in this film because-

00:01:17.861 --> 00:01:18.694
(audience applauds)

00:01:18.694 --> 00:01:20.313
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:01:20.313 --> 00:01:23.100
(audience applauds)

00:01:23.100 --> 00:01:24.660
- Just give me a part of something that

00:01:24.660 --> 00:01:27.600
can create opportunity for
like, these two young ladies.

00:01:27.600 --> 00:01:29.490
To see them in this film,

00:01:29.490 --> 00:01:31.565
makes my old dead heart feel very warm-

00:01:31.565 --> 00:01:33.523
(speakers laughing)

00:01:33.523 --> 00:01:34.448
We need more of that.

00:01:34.448 --> 00:01:35.406
We need more of them.

00:01:35.406 --> 00:01:37.140
- This is their film, you
know, the two of them.

00:01:37.140 --> 00:01:39.570
And for us to be able to support them

00:01:39.570 --> 00:01:41.812
in these roles where we're really just

00:01:41.812 --> 00:01:45.510
really amplifying their incredible talent.

00:01:45.510 --> 00:01:48.480
They carry this movie
and we're so proud to be

00:01:48.480 --> 00:01:51.150
a part of something that
shines a light on them and

00:01:51.150 --> 00:01:53.013
all of the young people on the film.

